window.NARRATION = {"ci_a": {"dur": 22.72, "text": "Pressure shows how you actually lead. This is where you start to see the gap between instinct and intention. Take about 30 seconds on each of these. Write what actually went on inside you, rather than what you think should have happened. Only you can see what you write, and it's saved here so you can come back to it. Select Save on each one as you go, then select Next.", "sents": [[0.03, "Pressure shows how you actually lead.", 0], [2.93, "This is where you start to see the gap between instinct and intention.", 0], [7.35, "Take about 30 seconds on each of these.", 1], [9.97, "Write what actually went on inside you, rather than what you think should have happened.", 1], [14.69, "Only you can see what you write, and it's saved here so you can come back to it.", 1], [19.05, "Select Save on each one as you go, then select Next.", 2]], "v": "k1", "cues": [0.03, 7.35, 19.05]}, "ci_b": {"dur": 10.8, "text": "Now look at what you wrote and pick the pattern that's closest to it. There's no right answer. Naming a habit helps you catch it sooner next time, so pick the one that best reflects your experience.", "sents": [[0.01, "Now look at what you wrote and pick the pattern that's closest to it.", 0], [3.75, "There's no right answer.", 1], [5.23, "Naming a habit helps you catch it sooner next time, so pick the one that best reflects your experience.", 1]], "v": "k1", "cues": [0.01, 3.75]}, "ci_c": {"dur": 20.08, "text": "Now run the Foundation Reset. Say your five words, the ones you saved on the Foundation Reset screen. Ask yourself for two next-best steps. Pick the one you'll take in the next ten minutes. Then take one breath and answer the anchor on the last card. It takes about a minute and works best standing up, so do it now before you move on.", "sents": [[0, "Now run the Foundation Reset.", 0], [2.15, "Say your five words, the ones you saved on the Foundation Reset screen.", 1], [6.37, "Ask yourself for two next-best steps.", 1], [9.07, "Pick the one you'll take in the next ten minutes.", 1], [11.71, "Then take one breath and answer the anchor on the last card.", 1], [15.41, "It takes about a minute and works best standing up, so do it now before you move on.", 2]], "v": "k1", "cues": [0, 2.15, 15.41]}, "kc_retry": {"dur": 3.68, "text": "Not quite. Have another look, then try again.", "sents": [[0.05, "Not quite.", 0], [1.45, "Have another look, then try again.", 0]], "v": "v4l", "cues": [0.05]}, "n_2_15": {"dur": 16.24, "text": "Time for the drill. The Moment gave you time to think. This drill gives you a few seconds under a little pressure to see how you respond. Press Play. The video stops a few times so you can answer, and it resumes when you're done. Your Playbook pages come right after.", "sents": [[0.01, "Time for the drill.", 0], [1.41, "The Moment gave you time to think.", 0], [3.67, "This drill gives you a few seconds under a little pressure to see how you respond.", 0], [8.43, "Press Play.", 1], [9.53, "The video stops a few times so you can answer, and it resumes when you're done.", 1], [14.11, "Your Playbook pages come right after.", 1]], "v": "k1", "cues": [0.01, 8.43]}, "pc_n_2_0": {"dur": 11.76, "text": "Lesson 2 is your scouting report, and it starts with you. You'll draft your own leadership blueprint, then learn how to respond when your Athleader shares something difficult. Select Start Lesson.", "sents": [[0, "Lesson 2 is your scouting report, and it starts with you.", 0], [3.91, "You'll draft your own leadership blueprint, then learn how to respond when your Athleader shares something difficult.", 1], [10.17, "Select Start Lesson.", 1]], "v": "r3", "cues": [0, 3.91]}, "pc_n_2_1": {"dur": 13.28, "text": "Read this moment, and picture yourself in it. That sentence is well meant, and it usually ends the conversation. This lesson gives you a different first sentence and asks you to do your own scouting report before theirs.", "sents": [[0.05, "Read this moment, and picture yourself in it.", 0], [3.49, "That sentence is well meant, and it usually ends the conversation.", 1], [7.69, "This lesson gives you a different first sentence and asks you to do your own scouting report before theirs.", 1]], "v": "r3L", "cues": [0.05, 3.49]}, "pc_n_2_10": {"dur": 11.6, "text": "Try this one. For each coaching line, decide whether it looks back or looks forward. Forward-looking lines still take the past seriously. They just end on what the person will do next.", "sents": [[0.03, "Try this one.", 0], [1.27, "For each coaching line, decide whether it looks back or looks forward.", 0], [5.83, "Forward-looking lines still take the past seriously.", 1], [9.19, "They just end on what the person will do next.", 1]], "v": "r3L", "cues": [0.03, 5.83]}, "pc_n_2_12": {"dur": 21.76, "text": "Here are the three steps from the video. First, acknowledge what they've noticed before offering guidance. It shows you heard them. Second, connect it to what's ahead. If they've found a strength, ask how they could use it on their ninety-day goal. Third, agree one small action and set a date. That's what turns a good conversation into something they own.", "sents": [[0.01, "Here are the three steps from the video.", 0], [2.33, "First, acknowledge what they've noticed before offering guidance.", 1], [6.39, "It shows you heard them.", 1], [7.97, "Second, connect it to what's ahead.", 2], [10.61, "If they've found a strength, ask how they could use it on their ninety-day goal.", 2], [14.87, "Third, agree one small action and set a date.", 3], [18.49, "That's what turns a good conversation into something they own.", 3]], "v": "pc1", "cues": [0.01, 2.33, 7.97, 14.87]}, "pc_n_2_13": {"dur": 6.56, "text": "Now try the feedback steps on a real line from a check-in. Pick the response you'd give, and you'll hear where it leads.", "sents": [[0, "Now try the feedback steps on a real line from a check-in.", 0], [3.49, "Pick the response you'd give, and you'll hear where it leads.", 1]], "v": "r3L", "cues": [0, 3.49]}, "pc_n_2_13_o0": {"dur": 9.68, "text": "It's positive, and it moves on too fast. Nothing was acknowledged, and a development plan isn't an action with a date. Try the other option to compare.", "sents": [[0, "It's positive, and it moves on too fast.", 0], [3.37, "Nothing was acknowledged, and a development plan isn't an action with a date.", 0], [7.99, "Try the other option to compare.", 0]], "v": "r3L", "cues": [0]}, "pc_n_2_13_o1": {"dur": 8.72, "text": "You acknowledged it, connected it to the month ahead and agreed one concrete action. That's the whole framework, and it took about ten seconds.", "sents": [[0.01, "You acknowledged it, connected it to the month ahead and agreed one concrete action.", 0], [5.29, "That's the whole framework, and it took about ten seconds.", 0]], "v": "r3L", "cues": [0.01]}, "pc_n_2_15": {"dur": 33.2, "text": "Your core rep this week happens inside a check-in you'd hold anyway: use the three feedback steps and notice whether your habit is to analyze the past or build the next move. If you have more time, draft your own M.V.P.+V. Brainstorm ten to fifteen values and keep three to five. Then draft your purpose, vision, and mission. Also, write the sentence you'll say when your Athleader shares something vulnerable, along with the question that follows it. Run your core rep, then ask your Athleader how it landed. Select Open your Lesson 2 pages to get started.", "sents": [[0.01, "Your core rep this week happens inside a check-in you'd hold anyway: use the three feedback steps and notice whether your habit is to analyze the past or build the next move.", 0], [10.35, "If you have more time, draft your own M.V.P.+V.", 1], [14.13, "Brainstorm ten to fifteen values and keep three to five.", 1], [17.83, "Then draft your purpose, vision, and mission.", 1], [20.89, "Also, write the sentence you'll say when your Athleader shares something vulnerable, along with the question that follows it.", 2], [27.29, "Run your core rep, then ask your Athleader how it landed.", 3], [30.53, "Select Open your Lesson 2 pages to get started.", 3]], "v": "pc1", "cues": [0.01, 10.35, 20.89, 27.29]}, "pc_n_2_16": {"dur": 12.72, "text": "This lesson's Athleader Pro is LaChina Robinson, the Pressure Player. She works as a basketball analyst and broadcaster, and she knows what it takes to stay flexible when the pressure's on. Press Play to hear from her.", "sents": [[0, "This lesson's Athleader Pro is LaChina Robinson, the Pressure Player.", 0], [4.89, "She works as a basketball analyst and broadcaster, and she knows what it takes to stay flexible when the pressure's on.", 1], [11.35, "Press Play to hear from her.", 1]], "v": "r3L", "cues": [0, 4.89]}, "pc_n_2_17": {"dur": 12.16, "text": "LaChina's drill helps you pivot under pressure and takes three minutes. Select Start the timer and work through each step. When you've completed the drill or scheduled a time to run it, select the option that fits.", "sents": [[0.07, "LaChina's drill helps you pivot under pressure and takes three minutes.", 0], [4.37, "Select Start the timer and work through each step.", 1], [7.59, "When you've completed the drill or scheduled a time to run it, select the option that fits.", 1]], "v": "pc1", "cues": [0.07, 4.37]}, "pc_n_2_19_q0": {"dur": 8.16, "text": "A few questions on the main ideas. First: why do you draft your own M.V.P.+V before coaching your Athleader through theirs?", "sents": [[0, "A few questions on the main ideas.", 0], [2.21, "First: why do you draft your own M.V.P.+V before coaching your Athleader through theirs?", 0]], "v": "r3", "cues": [0]}, "pc_n_2_19_q1": {"dur": 5.6, "text": "Your Athleader tells you about a setback. Which first response builds psychological safety?", "sents": [[0, "Your Athleader tells you about a setback.", 0], [2.69, "Which first response builds psychological safety?", 0]], "v": "r3L", "cues": [0]}, "pc_n_2_19_q2": {"dur": 2.88, "text": "What is the second step of forward-looking feedback?", "sents": [[0, "What is the second step of forward-looking feedback?", 0]], "v": "r3", "cues": [0]}, "pc_n_2_19_q3": {"dur": 6.4, "text": "Last one. Your Athleader only ever shares good news in check-ins. What's the best move?", "sents": [[0.15, "Last one.", 0], [1.27, "Your Athleader only ever shares good news in check-ins.", 0], [5.21, "What's the best move?", 0]], "v": "r3L", "cues": [0.15]}, "pc_n_2_19_w0": {"dur": 7.2, "text": "Doing it yourself shows you where it's hard and where it's vulnerable, which makes you a better coach when your Athleader shares theirs.", "sents": [[0, "Doing it yourself shows you where it's hard and where it's vulnerable, which makes you a better coach when your Athleader shares theirs.", 0]], "v": "r3", "cues": [0]}, "pc_n_2_19_w1": {"dur": 9.12, "text": "It thanks them for trusting you and hands the meaning back to them, without judging. Reassurance sounds kind, and it closes the topic just as fast.", "sents": [[0, "It thanks them for trusting you and hands the meaning back to them, without judging.", 0], [4.99, "Reassurance sounds kind, and it closes the topic just as fast.", 0]], "v": "r3", "cues": [0]}, "pc_n_2_19_w2": {"dur": 6.72, "text": "Acknowledge first, then connect the insight to what's ahead, and then agree on one action with a date.", "sents": [[0, "Acknowledge first, then connect the insight to what's ahead, and then agree on one action with a date.", 0]], "v": "pc1", "cues": [0]}, "pc_n_2_19_w3": {"dur": 8.24, "text": "Sharing something real first shows that setbacks are safe to talk about. Then an open question gives them room to do the same.", "sents": [[0.05, "Sharing something real first shows that setbacks are safe to talk about.", 0], [4.93, "Then an open question gives them room to do the same.", 0]], "v": "r3L", "cues": [0.05]}, "pc_n_2_20": {"dur": 36.88, "text": "Before you go, here's what to keep from this lesson. Your scouting report comes first. Draft your M.V.P.+V in your own words, however rough, before your Athleader shares theirs. When someone shares something hard, your first sentence decides whether they keep talking. Thank them, then ask. And feedback points forward: acknowledge, connect to what's next, and agree one action with a date. Select Download my answers for a Word document containing what you wrote today. If you'd like to go further, Chapter 8 of the book is about reading a setback the way a coach reads film.", "sents": [[0.03, "Before you go, here's what to keep from this lesson.", 0], [3.27, "Your scouting report comes first.", 1], [5.73, "Draft your M.V.P.+V in your own words, however rough, before your Athleader shares theirs.", 1], [12.39, "When someone shares something hard, your first sentence decides whether they keep talking.", 2], [17.39, "Thank them, then ask.", 2], [18.17, "And feedback points forward: acknowledge, connect to what's next, and agree one action with a date.", 3], [24.09, "Select Download my answers for a Word document containing what you wrote today.", 4], [31.09, "If you'd like to go further, Chapter 8 of the book is about reading a setback the way a coach reads film.", 4]], "v": "pc1", "cues": [0.03, 3.27, 12.39, 18.17, 24.09]}, "pc_n_2_21": {"dur": 16.72, "text": "That's Lesson 2 done. Keep going? Your coaching is already changing. This week, run your core rep: use the three feedback steps in your next check-in and ask how it landed. Next time, you'll set one ninety-day goal for your own leadership and then help your team choose theirs.", "sents": [[0, "That's Lesson 2 done.", 0], [1.63, "Keep going?", 0], [2.51, "Your coaching is already changing.", 0], [5.11, "This week, run your core rep: use the three feedback steps in your next check-in and ask how it landed.", 1], [11.31, "Next time, you'll set one ninety-day goal for your own leadership and then help your team choose theirs.", 1]], "v": "pc1", "cues": [0, 5.11]}, "pc_n_2_3": {"dur": 6.24, "text": "A quick look back at Lesson 1 before you start. Choose the answer you remember. This one isn't scored.", "sents": [[0, "A quick look back at Lesson 1 before you start.", 0], [2.93, "Choose the answer you remember.", 1], [4.69, "This one isn't scored.", 1]], "v": "r3L", "cues": [0, 2.93]}, "pc_n_2_4": {"dur": 35.68, "text": "Here's what you'll practice in this lesson. You'll draft your own M.V.P.+V: your mission, vision, purpose, and values. Your Athleader starts the same work this week with their values and finishes it in Lesson 3. Yours goes first. When your Athleader shares something vulnerable, you'll have one sentence ready that thanks them and one curious question that follows it. You'll learn a three-step way to give feedback that points forward: Acknowledge the insight, connect it to what's next, and agree one action. And you'll use it in a real check-in with your Athleader. That's your core rep this week.", "sents": [[0.01, "Here's what you'll practice in this lesson.", 0], [2.29, "You'll draft your own M.V.P.+V: your mission, vision, purpose, and values.", 1], [6.77, "Your Athleader starts the same work this week with their values and finishes it in Lesson 3.", 1], [13.75, "Yours goes first.", 1], [15.31, "When your Athleader shares something vulnerable, you'll have one sentence ready that thanks them and one curious question that follows it.", 2], [22.57, "You'll learn a three-step way to give feedback that points forward: Acknowledge the insight, connect it to what's next, and agree one action.", 3], [30.93, "And you'll use it in a real check-in with your Athleader.", 4], [34.13, "That's your core rep this week.", 4]], "v": "r3L", "cues": [0.01, 2.29, 15.31, 22.57, 30.93]}, "pc_n_2_7": {"dur": 19.92, "text": "M.V.P. stands for mission, vision, and purpose, plus V for your values. You build it from the foundation up: purpose first, then your vision and your mission, with your values underneath all three. Your Playbook has a page for each one. Select each one to hear what it asks of you. Open all four before you move on.", "sents": [[0.01, "M.V.P. stands for mission, vision, and purpose, plus V for your values.", 0], [5.45, "You build it from the foundation up: purpose first, then your vision and your mission, with your values underneath all three.", 0], [12.83, "Your Playbook has a page for each one.", 0], [15.25, "Select each one to hear what it asks of you.", 1], [17.85, "Open all four before you move on.", 1]], "v": "o11", "cues": [0.01, 15.25]}, "pc_n_2_7_mission": {"dur": 10.08, "text": "Your mission is how you get there, day to day. Write it as one sentence: what you'll do, for whom, by focusing on what, to get which result.", "sents": [[0.01, "Your mission is how you get there, day to day.", 0], [3.35, "Write it as one sentence: what you'll do, for whom, by focusing on what, to get which result.", 0]], "v": "r3", "cues": [0.01]}, "pc_n_2_7_purpose": {"dur": 8.8, "text": "Your purpose is your why. It's the lasting impact you want to have as a leader, and it should still be true if your title changed tomorrow.", "sents": [[0.01, "Your purpose is your why.", 0], [2.39, "It's the lasting impact you want to have as a leader, and it should still be true if your title changed tomorrow.", 0]], "v": "r3L", "cues": [0.01]}, "pc_n_2_7_values": {"dur": 12.88, "text": "Your values are the three to five foundations you come back to daily, and they shape your actions. Remember the executive in the video: her value was creativity, and a purely administrative role was draining her.", "sents": [[0.01, "Your values are the three to five foundations you come back to daily, and they shape your actions.", 0], [6.17, "Remember the executive in the video: her value was creativity, and a purely administrative role was draining her.", 0]], "v": "r3L", "cues": [0.01]}, "pc_n_2_7_vision": {"dur": 8.4, "text": "Your vision is where your leadership is heading, three to five years out. Picture the team you lead then, and what the people on it have become.", "sents": [[0.05, "Your vision is where your leadership is heading, three to five years out.", 0], [4.71, "Picture the team you lead then, and what the people on it have become.", 0]], "v": "r3L", "cues": [0.05]}, "pc_n_2_9": {"dur": 29.84, "text": "Here's the example from the video, side by side. An employee shares a failure with their manager. It's a vulnerable moment. Manager A tells them what they should have done. It's advice, and it lands as judgment, so the conversation stops there. Manager B thanks them and asks what it taught them. The employee does the thinking, and they're likely to bring the next story, too. Your first sentence decides whether you hear the second story. Your Playbook asks you to write yours down before the check-in.", "sents": [[0.03, "Here's the example from the video, side by side.", 0], [3.31, "An employee shares a failure with their manager.", 1], [6.33, "It's a vulnerable moment.", 1], [8.19, "Manager A tells them what they should have done.", 2], [10.81, "It's advice, and it lands as judgment, so the conversation stops there.", 2], [15.55, "Manager B thanks them and asks what it taught them.", 3], [18.87, "The employee does the thinking, and they're likely to bring the next story, too.", 3], [22.83, "Your first sentence decides whether you hear the second story.", 4], [26.51, "Your Playbook asks you to write yours down before the check-in.", 4]], "v": "r3", "cues": [0.03, 3.31, 8.19, 15.55, 22.83]}, "r2_code_pulse": {"dur": 7.36, "text": "Type the code from the last page of the Pulse Check, then select Submit. A quick knowledge check comes next, then your recap.", "sents": [[0.01, "Type the code from the last page of the Pulse Check, then select Submit.", 0], [4.23, "A quick knowledge check comes next, then your recap.", 0]], "v": "r3", "cues": [0.01]}, "r2_form_pulse": {"dur": 8.96, "text": "Answer the five questions, then select Submit. Your code appears on the last page. Copy the code or write it down, then select Next.", "sents": [[0, "Answer the five questions, then select Submit.", 0], [3.25, "Your code appears on the last page.", 0], [5.45, "Copy the code or write it down, then select Next.", 0]], "v": "r3", "cues": [0]}, "r2_pulse": {"dur": 21.36, "text": "Every lesson has the same short Pulse Check, a check-in that helps you see how you're changing over the season. It asks how often you've practiced each of the Core 4 and completed your reps in the last two weeks. It takes about a minute, and your answers go to the Athleadership team, who use them to see how the whole group is progressing. Select Next, and it opens right here.", "sents": [[0.01, "Every lesson has the same short Pulse Check, a check-in that helps you see how you're changing over the season.", 0], [6.57, "It asks how often you've practiced each of the Core 4 and completed your reps in the last two weeks.", 1], [12.25, "It takes about a minute, and your answers go to the Athleadership team, who use them to see how the whole group is progressing.", 2], [18.83, "Select Next, and it opens right here.", 2]], "v": "k1", "cues": [0.01, 6.57, 12.25]}};
